     by default"), rather than "the scalar functions of no other family";
  3. functions.h's block is cut: the add-builtin-function skill holds
     both definition forms and the wrapping rule; the why of the wrapping
     (ambiguous lookup under `using namespace sqlite_orm;`) is added to
     the skill's wrapping line; window.h's paragraphs 2 and 3 likewise
     (source-layout.md, vocabulary-layer.md:310);
  4. fts5_deprecations.h: the rank() dual meaning onto the deprecated
     order_by(rank()), the is_equal<Table> passage onto its factory, "Goes
     as a whole in v1.11" cut (each factory's notice says it); the
     header-of-its-own reason goes into the Intention;
  5. fts5_functions.h's passage onto fts5::hidden::any's doc-comment
     (fts5.h), the one declaration it concerns, its `///` line turned into
     a `/** */` block;
  6. links on the public structs and factories lacking one: the next
     commit.
- trueqbit: the headers that gather say "umbrella", as node_traits.h and
  node_algorithms.h do: functions.h and dbos.h.
- Rule 15: "function" and "collation" read otherwise in C++: the families
  say "SQL function"; collations.h takes SQLite's "collating functions"
  (datatype3.html#collation: "built-in collating functions: BINARY,
